<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico details secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico details secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 9.068 billion pesos from the secondary market on Thursday through a combination of direct sales of government paper and repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The sales of government paper were offered as follows:</p>
<p>	 AMOUNT     TERM</p>
<p>     100 million   350 days</p>
<p>     100 million   182 days</p>
<p>     100 million    91 days</p>
<p>The repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM</p>
<p>1.500 bln  19 days</p>
<p>1.500 bln  15 days</p>
<p>1.000 bln  13 days</p>
<p>1.000 bln  12 days</p>
<p>600 million  11 days</p>
<p>	600 million   8 days</p>
<p>	600 million   7 days</p>
<p>	600 million   5 days</p>
<p>    1.500 bln   1 day</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
